"},{"name":"Penny Wong","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10678","person_slug":"penny-wong","vote":"no"},{"name":"Perin Davey","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10947","person_slug":"perin-davey","vote":"no"},{"name":"Peter Whish-Wilson","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Raff Ciccone","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10915","person_slug":"raff-ciccone","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ralph Babet","party":"United Australia Party","person_id":"tvfy_11003","person_slug":"ralph-babet","vote":"no"},{"name":"Richard Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Henderson","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10790","person_slug":"sarah-henderson","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steph Hodgins-May","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_11020","person_slug":"steph-hodgins-may","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Susan McDonald","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10951","person_slug":"susan-mcdonald","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tammy Tyrrell","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_11012","person_slug":"tammy-tyrrell","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tim Ayres","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10946","person_slug":"tim-ayres","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tony Sheldon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10944","person_slug":"tony-sheldon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Varun Ghosh","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11017","person_slug":"varun-ghosh","vote":"no"}],"name":"Wage Justice for Early Childhood Education and Care Workers (Special Account) Bill 2024 - Second Reading - First Nations self-determination","noes":33,"question":"The majority voted against an [amendment](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?gid=2024-11-26.302.1) to the usual second reading motion, which is \"*that the bill be read a second time*\" (parliamentary jargon for agreeing with the main idea of the bill). The amendment was introduced by Victorian Senator [Lidia Thorpe](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/victoria/lidia_thorpe) (Greens). ### Amendment text > *At the end of the motion, add \", but the Senate:* > > *(a) notes:* > >> *(i) more than 22,900 Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander children and young people are in out-of-home care,* >> >> *(ii) the child protection system, which was built to remove children from their families, continues to inflict harm on First Nations families,* >> >> *(iii) the Productivity Commission's inquiry report, A path to universal early childhood education and care, has found that governments continue to fail on their commitments to shared decision making and supporting the community-controlled sector,* >> >> *(iv) improving outcomes for First Nations communities starts with supporting children and allowing First Nations communities to self-determine their own solutions for caring for young people; and* > > *(b) calls on the Government to:* > >> *(i) commit to shared decision making and handing over control of services for First Nations young people and families to the community-controlled sector,* >> >> *(ii) ensure accountability in funding for early years by prioritising community-controlled organisations delivering services and outcomes for families, and* >> >> *(iii) provide additional supports for smaller early years organisations to develop their own enterprise agreements\".*","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-9276","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2024-11-26/24"}
